{
  "schema_version": "1.9.2",
  "id": "USN-9214-1",
  "summary": "binutils vulnerabilities",
  "details": "It was discovered that the GNU binutils gold linker incorrectly handled\ncertain ELF files. A local attacker could possibly use this issue to cause\nGNU binutils to crash, resulting in a denial of service. This issue only\naffected Ubuntu 22.04 LTS. (CVE-2019-1010204)\n\nHan Zheng discovered that GNU binutils incorrectly handled demangling\ncertain Rust symbols. A local attacker could possibly use this issue to\ncause GNU binutils to crash, resulting in a denial of service. This issue\nonly affected Ubuntu 22.04 LTS. (CVE-2022-27943)\n\nIt was discovered that GNU binutils incorrectly handled certain DWARF debug\ninformation. A local attacker could possibly use this issue to cause GNU\nbinutils to use excessive resources, leading to a denial of service. This\nissue only affected Ubuntu 22.04 LTS. (CVE-2022-48064)\n\nIt was discovered that the GNU binutils linker did not properly free memory\nunder certain circumstances. A local attacker could possibly use this issue\nto cause GNU binutils to use excessive resources, leading to a denial of\nservice. This issue only affected Ubuntu 22.04 LTS and Ubuntu 24.04 LTS.\n(CVE-2025-1150)\n\nIt was discovered that the GNU binutils linker incorrectly handled certain\nTLS relocations on x86 systems, leading to a heap-based buffer overflow. A\nlocal attacker could possibly use this issue to cause GNU binutils to\ncrash, resulting in a denial of service. This issue only affected Ubuntu\n22.04 LTS and Ubuntu 24.04 LTS. (CVE-2025-11495)\n\nIt was discovered that GNU binutils incorrectly handled certain malformed\nDWARF debug information, leading to an infinite loop. A local attacker\ncould possibly use these issues to cause GNU binutils to use excessive\nresources, leading to a denial of service. These issues only affected\nUbuntu 24.04 LTS. (CVE-2025-69644, CVE-2025-69646)\n\nIt was discovered that GNU binutils incorrectly handled certain malformed\nDWARF debug information. A local attacker could possibly use these issues\nto cause GNU binutils to crash, resulting in a denial of service. These\nissues only affected Ubuntu 22.04 LTS and Ubuntu 24.04 LTS.\n(CVE-2025-69645, CVE-2025-69652)\n\nIt was discovered that GNU binutils incorrectly handled certain XCOFF\nobject files, leading to out-of-bounds reads. A local attacker could\npossibly use these issues to cause GNU binutils to crash, resulting in a\ndenial of service, or obtain sensitive information. (CVE-2026-3441,\nCVE-2026-3442, CVE-2026-4647, CVE-2026-15003)\n\nIt was discovered that the GNU binutils linker incorrectly handled certain\nXCOFF object files, leading to a heap-based buffer overflow. A local\nattacker could possibly use this issue to cause GNU binutils to crash,\nresulting in a denial of service, or possibly execute arbitrary code.\n(CVE-2026-6846)\n\nIt was discovered that the GNU binutils linker incorrectly handled memory\nwhen a linker plugin claimed an archive member, leading to a\nuse-after-free. A local attacker could possibly use this issue to cause GNU\nbinutils to crash, resulting in a denial of service, or possibly execute\narbitrary code. (CVE-2026-19548)\n\nIt was discovered that the GNU binutils linker incorrectly handled certain\ninvalid relocations on x86 systems, leading to a buffer overflow. A local\nattacker could possibly use this issue to cause GNU binutils to crash,\nresulting in a denial of service. (CVE-2026-90803)\n\nIt was discovered that the GNU binutils linker incorrectly handled certain\norphan sections. A local attacker could possibly use this issue to cause\nGNU binutils to crash, resulting in a denial of service. This issue only\naffected Ubuntu 24.04 LTS and Ubuntu 26.04 LTS. (CVE-2026-90828)\n\nIt was discovered that the GNU binutils linker incorrectly handled certain\nobject files on x86 systems, leading to NULL pointer dereferences. A local\nattacker could possibly use these issues to cause GNU binutils to crash,\nresulting in a denial of service. (CVE-2026-91781, CVE-2026-91782)",
